%N A400189 Walk along the hexagonal spiral, with its cells numbered starting at 0, as in A395362. Three players, Black, Cyan, and Red, take turns. When it is Black's's turn, he places a (Glinski) queen at the smallest unoccupied cell not attacked by an existing Cyan or Red queen; when it is Cyan's turn, he places a queen at the smallest unoccupied cell not attacked by an existing Black or Red queen, and when it is Red's turn, he places a queen at the smallest unoccupied cell not attacked by an existing Black or Cyan queen. Sequence lists the unoccupied cells.
%H A400189 Jonas Karlsson, <a href="/A400189/b400189.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..9999</a>
%H A400189 Jonas Karlsson, <a href="/A400186/a400186.png">The first million queens in the spiral</a>
%H A400189 Jonas Karlsson, <a href="/A400186/a400186_1.png">The first ten million queens in the spiral</a>
%Y A400189 Cf. A400186, A400187, A400188, A396292. For queens of two colors, see A396294, A396295, A396296.
